From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] variant: declare _os_xbs_chrooted

variant.c reads _os_xbs_chrooted, which libsystem_kernel defines in
wrappers/_libkernel_init.c, but no published header declares it: Apple's
build takes the declaration from an internal header. Declare it where it is
used, as libpthread patch 0001 does.

Rebase-risk: low (one declaration).
---
diff --git a/libdarwin/variant.c b/libdarwin/variant.c
--- a/libdarwin/variant.c
+++ b/libdarwin/variant.c
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@
 #include <os/stdlib.h>
 #include <os/variant_private.h>
 #include <os/boot_mode_private.h>
+
+// Set by libsystem_kernel (_libkernel_init.c) when running chrooted in a build
+// environment; Apple declares it in an unpublished header.
+extern bool _os_xbs_chrooted;
 
 /*
  * Lists all properties overridden by an empty file
